      "message": "Checking blocksA.size() \u003e MAX_RENDER_BLOCKS (and blocksB.size() \u003e MAX_RENDER_BLOCKS on line 319) before activeBudget.tryConsumeBlocks(...) short-circuits cumulative block accounting on oversize-block files. Because rendered stays false in recordOutcome, a multi-file commit of small micro-block files (\u003e25k blocks each) leaves blocksUsed at 0 and exhausted false, bypassing the 32,000-block request cap until hitting the scan or CPU limit. Call !activeBudget.tryConsumeBlocks(...) first on both sides so oversize-block files are still charged against the request budget.",
